WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:06.720
SCP-682, the indestructible reptile, versus&nbsp;
SCP-3519, a dangerous memetic contagion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:11.120
responsible for killing nearly the entire&nbsp;
population of the world. In a certain timeline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:16.640
SCP-3519 infected global media to influence the&nbsp;
public into believing that the world would end on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:18.560
March 5th, 2019, and that self-destruction was a&nbsp;
preferable option. Weeks before March 5th, a group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:23.040
of Foundation personnel decided&nbsp;
to test 3519’s exposure with 682,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:28.160
in hopes that it may terminate the lizard once and&nbsp;
for all. Lowering the acid levels inside its tank,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:33.520
682 was exposed to the contagion, but did not&nbsp;
show any self-destructive ideation. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:38.960
682 nightmarishly laughed for 193 seconds&nbsp;
before it was placed back into containment.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.080
After March 5th, there was&nbsp;
only one lone human survivor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:46.560
Junior Researcher Dr. Rory Jones. When&nbsp;
682 encountered the Doctor after breaching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:50.160
containment, it did not kill him.
Instead, it simply stated:&nbsp;

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:55.280
“We are alike now, meat. Killing&nbsp;
you would only end suffering.”

